<title>POLAND: Stalexport to vote on bonds Dec 21.</title>
<headline>Stalexport to vote on bonds Dec 21.</headline>
<dateline>WARSAW 1996-11-29</dateline>
<text>
<p>Shareholders of Polish steel trader Stalexport SA will vote on December 21 on whether to issue convertible bonds and shares for which they can be exchanged, the firm said in a statement on Friday.</p>
<p>It gave no details.</p>
<p>Last week the daily Parkiet reported that the firm was considering a $50 million issue that was likely to take place in February next year and be placed abroad.</p>
<p>Stalexport currently has 8,833,826 shares outstanding. @</p>
<p>Its main shareholders are the treasury with a 25 percent stake, the Merkury Investment Association with a 10.65 percent stake and Creditanstalt Bankverein with 5.55 percent.</p>
<p>-- Warsaw Newsroom +48 22 653 9700</p>
